  "description": "Mechanical joining with rivets — permanent fasteners installed through holes in overlapping plates. Hot rivets contract on cooling, producing preload that makes joints leak-tight and vibration-resistant. Dominated structural steel construction from ~1840 until arc welding replaced riveting after ~1940.",
